---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Privy: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Assess the Privy migration route after Yotpo messaging retirement, with destination-specific acceptance checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I keep sending through Yotpo during this migration?",
    "answer": "Do not plan on it. The messaging login reports decommissioned dashboard and background services. Confirm available records with support; do not promise a retired-sender rollback."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the key Privy acceptance decision?",
    "answer": "Verify that display intent, migration imports and rebuilt flows produce different appropriate enrollment."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do Reviews and Loyalty move with messaging?",
    "answer": "Treat them as separate services and data dependencies. Name the owner of review requests and points messages, and verify any required destination integration."
  },
  {
    "question": "Were the migration checks on this page performed?",
    "answer": "No. They are proposed checks for a receiving account. Production delivery, permissions, recovery and account-specific costs require separate validation."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <nav><a class="link" href="/apps">Tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">Selection framework</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS is a migration question now. Its messaging login reports that the application and background services are decommissioned. Reviews and Loyalty are separate decisions. An old export or implementation guide does not prove that a retired dashboard can still be opened. Privy evaluation should join storefront capture to the receiving email and SMS flows. A popup replacement alone does not establish that migrated customers enter the right journeys.</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Separate advertised migration help from an agreed scope</h2>
      <p>Privy’s <a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/comparison/yotpo">Yotpo migration page</a> advertises help moving contacts, templates and automations for email and SMS. It is a marketing offer, not an account-specific migration specification. Ask for the included objects, exclusions, available source files and acceptance responsibilities in writing.</p>
      <p>Do not use the dated promotional discount on that page as a current quote. Request pricing for your actual audience, channels and service needs. No order-count threshold determines whether Privy is sufficient: the deciding requirements are the workflows your team needs to operate.</p>
      <h2>Map signup intent through each live display</h2>
      <p>List the storefront displays still present: newsletter popup, launch waitlist, cart incentive and checkout marketing choice. For each, record its promise, channel permission, source property and intended first message. Replace obsolete Yotpo destinations and verify that the new form records the same intent.</p>
      <p>Proposed acceptance case: a launch-waitlist signup should receive launch context, while an ordinary newsletter signup should receive its promised welcome. Inspect both records and queues. A shared discount flow that erases signup intent fails this test even if the profile appears immediately.</p>
      <h2>Import returning customers without another acquisition reward</h2>
      <p>Keep migration imports distinct from fresh display submissions. Preserve original signup evidence, channel statuses and suppressions. Before sending, inspect a returning purchaser, a recent unsubscribed contact and a newly collected subscriber. They should not all receive the same acquisition sequence.</p>
      <p>Use a staff-controlled existing profile to check whether a later popup submission overwrites a migration tag or channel status. Repeat after opting out. Document the receiving behavior and repair ambiguous rules before activating a large audience; profile deduplication alone does not demonstrate correct enrollment.</p>
      <h2>Translate templates and account for retained Yotpo modules</h2>
      <p>Ask the migration team to show one rebuilt cart flow and one post-purchase flow in the destination. Check trigger, purchase exit, product link, discount validity and template fallback. A screenshot resembling the old email does not prove its conditions were migrated.</p>
      <p>If Reviews or Loyalty remains with Yotpo, list exactly which data each Privy flow requires and request a current sample. Never promise full points or review history from a general migration offer. Proposed check: a customer awaiting a review invitation should have a single invitation owner and no duplicate discount sequence.</p>
      <h2>Release checklist, costs and evidence limits</h2>
      <p>Keep destination sends paused until eligible counts, suppressions, capture routes and representative queues reconcile. Name one owner for every automated message across Shopify, retained Yotpo modules and the receiving stack. If a destination check fails, pause that destination queue and repair it; the retired Yotpo sender is not a rollback option.</p>
      <p>Compare the receiving subscription, messaging usage, implementation work and retained Reviews or Loyalty costs. Sequenzy or another email service belongs in that budget only if its required integration and operating role are demonstrated. There is no evidenced universal winner or fixed price here.</p>
      <p>Checked against primary supplier material on 24 November 2026 and the <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommission notice</a>. These are proposed acceptance cases, not performed merchant tests. Historical data recovery, legal sufficiency, account entitlements and production delivery remain unverified. Related migration assessments: <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Omnisend</a>, <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript">Postscript</a>, <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy">Privy</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
